 This Warren Buffett dividend stock is crushing the market in 2026
 Andreja Stojanovic
 Stocks 
 Nov 2, 2026
 Share 
 Coca-Cola (NYSE: KO ) has, over the decades, proven to be one of the more lucrative stocks favored by the legendary investor Warren Buffett , both in terms of returns and its dividend yield. 
 Indeed, KO shares have rallied approximately 3,500% since 1988 – the year the Oracle of Omaha first started buying – and have also offered strong performance in 2026. Specifically, after starting the year at $69.12, Coca-Cola equity rose 36.52% to its press-time price of $94.36.
 A trader who put $1,000 in mid-1988 following Buffett would, therefore, have $36,000 at press time on Monday, November 2.
 Advertisement
 KO stock price YTD chart. Source: Google 
 Here’s how much Berkshire Hathaway is up on its KO stock investment in 2026
 Considering such performance and the fact that the fourth-quarter (Q4) 2025 13-f filing for Berkshire Hathaway (NYSE: BRK.A , BRK.B ) reveals that the conglomerate held 400 million KO shares worth approximately $27.96 billion at the start of 2026, Buffett is up more than $10 billion on the investment in the last 11 months. 
 A retail investor who purchased $1,000 worth of the equity on January 2 would have, meanwhile, gained $365.20 for a position worth $1,365.20 at press time on Monday, November 2.
 For comparison, the S&P 500 benchmark stock market index rallied a far smaller 11.06% year-to-date (YTD), and Pepsi (NASDAQ: PEP ), Coca-Cola’s most famous rival , fell 3.03% YTD.
 Coca-Cola (KO) stock dividend in 2026
 Meanwhile, KO stock is also known as a reliable dividend pick . For example, the company distributed a total of $1.59 per share so far in 2026 – $0.53 on April 1, July 1, and October 1, each – and is due to pay an additional $0.53 on December 15.
 Thus, Warren Buffett’s Berkshire Hathaway already received $636 million in yield this year and will have received a total of $848 million by 2027, provided the upcoming 13-f filings don’t reveal a reduction or increase in the firm’s Coca-Cola stake.
 A regular investor who purchased, for example, 100 shares at the start of 2026 would have received $159 by press time and would have received $212 by the next New Year’s Day for a $6,912 initial investment.
